; lang.xon -- what this bundle IS.

(lang "coreutils")

; THE X DIALECT, NOT RADON -- measured (2026-09-02).  The doors these
; applets need (File, Sys, Proc, Date) import on the plain dialect; the
; radon dialect boots the whole numeric tower and JIT-compiles its
; tokenizer analysers, none of which a tool uses, and that costs the
; difference between a 12-second `ls` and a 3-second one.  A tool that
; runs per file in a build cannot afford the tower.  Self-contained
; like x-make: the tool tier chains no dependencies.  One bundle, many
; applets -- the busybox shape: `x -l coreutils -- sort -u file`.
(dialect x)

(requires-release "v0.10.0")

(entry "run.x")
